NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator.classifyRelation kind=method
  digest=b3:fd978a3445343016a152c1ca78a9ba5a2b979e8ca711d63ba40298c58ad04a9c file=neo/internal/writeback/consolidator.go range=378:415 lang=go exported=false byte_range=16491:17893
  sig=func (c *Consolidator) classifyRelation(ctx context.Context, newText string, candidates []memory.Neighbor) (memory.Relation, string, string)
  doc=classifyRelation implements memory.RelationClassifier using the cheap\nconsolidation model. It is passed to the Remember*Related write paths and\ninvoked only when a similar neighbor exists. On any model/parse error it\nreturns RelationNew (no edge), so a flaky classifier degrades to the plain\nv1 write rather than mislinking memories.
EDGES
