NODE id=matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator.proposeIfReady kind=method
  digest=b3:9230f6c8b26ba65ac773c63c069260e6ef6f71fffc2fb9e67425595dd5c19547 file=neo/internal/writeback/consolidator.go range=111:144 lang=go exported=false byte_range=4379:5454
  sig=func (c *Consolidator) proposeIfReady(spec memory.PatternSpec, coverage int)
  doc=proposeIfReady checks if a pattern has accumulated enough successes\n(coverage >= cfg.MinPatternSuccesses) to be PROPOSED as a candidate skill.\nThis is the auto-propose extension (P2-2): when a successful tool-sequence\nrepeats past the existing confidence/N-success guard, the consolidator\nrecords the pattern's name as a proposed skill. Deduped by name (the dedup\nkey). Below the guard, nothing happens (anti-overfit). Nil-safe.
EDGES
  ^contains=matrix/neo/internal/writeback.Consolidator
  ^defines=matrix/neo/internal/writeback/consolidator.go

